{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1388348-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice","id":1388348,"title":"Coterie Embraced a Kinfolk: Advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-14T09:49:07-07:00","id":1388348,"title":"Coterie Embraced a Kinfolk: Advice","content":"In the game I run my players threw a curve at me. A friend of the teen that they're Guardian/Adopted parent of was suffering nightmares, bouts of temper, feeling like they were being watched. The kid was a kinfolk on the verge of turning into a garou and their first change and was being observed by a pack of bone gnawers.<br /> <br /> The idea was they would take the kid in for a few days, keep an eye on him, get attacked, and either fend off the lupines or, more likely, take the kid and run from these mysterious pursuers. They would harry and herd them and then when they were pinned he would undergo his first change and they would subdue him and then the older lupines would take him away.<br /> <br /> Instead, thinking the kid was marked and now both the kid and their teen were in the know about things supernatural and what little they did know about lupines being that they can be relentless, decided to embrace them to give them an edge in survival. I figured it would be a slim chance that the embrace would stick, kinfolk being resilient/blessed against such things. I rolled and the kid survived the embrace.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and opinions would be welcome. What would the lupine's response be? Retaliation and rage seems appropriate, but what scale? Full on war? Does this include just that one pack or does it include all of the bone gnawers in the Culver City/Greater Los Angeles area? Also, what about the other vampires in the area? Will it drag others into the mess?<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> PS: I thought this was implied, but just for context, the kid didn't know he was kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T15:02:26-07:00","id":1388445,"title":"","content":"If your players really embraced a kinfolk that whas promized to be a Garou then your players better change the continent while cleaning their tracks. For the Garou such a thing is one of the greatest offendings and as long they have a track they will go and bring their corrupted family member peace while erridicating those that have done this sacrileg. For the kid being unknown that it is kinfolk is actually the only good thing because then it will see the Garou as horrendous beast instead of feeling disgusted by what it have become.<br /> The kid would be better of covering the mark because while other garou would not follow them with such dedication they would still not keep still if they found out one of the kinfolk being corrupted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":".  Something to add 05-14-2020, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,",